 engineered components to original equipment manufacturers. The company serves heavy and medium duty commercial vehicles, construction and access equipment, powersports, data center and critical power, agriculture, military, and other end markets. Mayville Engineering Company, Inc. was founded in 1945 and is headquartered in Milwaukee, Wisconsin.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jagadeesh A. Reddy | President, CEO & Director | Age 53 | Compensation: $803,288 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $228K ranks in the bottom quartile among Industrials peers. Each employee generates $11K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $1K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Mayville Engineering Company, I is a small-cap industrials business with a $327M market cap on $546M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +0% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 8% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $27M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 5 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin -0.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.4%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 23% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":